    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0229" n="219" xml:id="pg219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-01T17:00:00+08:00">April 1, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:02 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>687. Embassy concurs with Peiping telegram 526, March 31 sent Department re
                    denial American participation in sinking <hi rendition="#italic">Chungking</hi>
                    and is prepared issue appropriate denial if Department so instructs.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 687, repeated Shanghai 317.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
